Add extra DTB build targets and their device tree sources for
meson8-minix-neo-x8h, meson8-mxiii and meson8m2-m8s-dvfs.

Rebased for kernel 6.20: arch/arm/boot/dts/Makefile no longer holds a
flat per-SoC dtb-y list -- it was refactored tree-wide into per-vendor
subdirectories, so the dtb-y list for Meson8/Meson8b/Meson8m2 now lives
in arch/arm/boot/dts/amlogic/Makefile. That list has also gained a new
entry (meson8-fernsehfee3.dtb) and been reordered since the original
6.1.51 baseline, so insertion points were re-derived from the current
file rather than reused verbatim.

The three new .dts source files (plus the meson8-mxiii.dtsi they
partially depend on) did not exist anywhere in the 6.20 tree -- they
originate from the (excluded, in this rebase) xdl-vs-mainline patch.
Sources were taken as-is from
../linux-m8x/debian-latest/debian/dtb/{meson8-minix-neo-x8h.dts,
meson8-mxiii.dts,meson8-mxiii.dtsi,meson8m2-m8s-dvfs.dts} and added
here as new files so the dtb-y entries below actually build. Their
own #include dependencies (meson8.dtsi, meson8m2-m8s.dts) already
exist in this tree.

Rebased once more for kernel 6.12.96: same situation as the 6.20 rebase
above (meson8-fernsehfee3.dtb still doesn't exist on this kernel
version either), so the new entries were re-inserted against the
current Makefile contents instead of reusing the 6.20-era hunk.

